00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:56,437
get out of here from the
east side of the building.

262
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,600
Are we agreed?

263
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,360
We should want safety.

264
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:07,359
We should make that our exit point.

265
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:12,237
I didn't expect the green child.

266
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,317
How did it ever come to this?

267
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:17,080
I had only the barest of information.

268
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:22,257
I have one job and it's simple:
get rid of Jolene Kujo permanently.

269
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:23,877
That's all I'm here for.

270
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:26,660
I just have to make sure I do that.

271
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,570
Damn it.

272
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,277
Where did Jolene and
those other two fools go?

273
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,478
Did they possibly manage to
escape and I missed them?

274
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,030
No.

275
00:16:40,113 --> 00:16:43,248
There's no way they could get
outside without my seeing them.

276
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,340
Hey, you.

277
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:45,991
What are you doing there?

278
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:49,200
Hey, I asked you a question.

279
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:50,997
Where are the other three?

280
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:53,668
And why haven't you
turned into a plant yet?

281
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,060
I'm in agony!

282
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:08,107
They modified a human
body into a death trap!

283
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,640
It hurts!

284
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:21,360
I've never felt such pain!

285
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:25,917
This is horrible!

286
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,680
I want my mama!

287
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:30,740
My left arm is useless now!

288
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:33,600
That was an awful experience.

289
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:37,297
Tailed Snake told me to make
them fight using Survivor,

290
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:41,760
and I'm pretty sure I did that,
but what really matters now is yay,

291
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:45,480
finally, I could go
outside and be in the sun.

292
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:59,081
That was close, but it looks like we made
a clean getaway from the other stand user.

293
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:00,935
Look, it's withering.

294
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:03,533
I guess it was a temporary thing anyway.

295
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:06,857
The bigger problem to worry
about is that at any minute,

296
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:10,297
prison staffers are going to realize
what happened at this discipline ward.

297
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,792
That's better for us, because if they do,

298
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:15,397
Palesnake will realize
that at the same time.

299
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:17,951
And he'll come out and show his ugly face.

300
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:22,258
Which then gives me the best chance
to take my dad's memory disc back.

301
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:26,940
Cholene, look!

302
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,240
Stone Ocean!

303
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:44,057
It's an enemy stand!

304
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:47,277
It's probably the one that
belongs to that guy playing army!

305
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,600
He took the fruit!

306
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,272
I won't let him have it!

307
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,780
Tiger, drive!

308
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,217
What's going on?

309
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:06,130
This body...

310
00:19:06,213 --> 00:19:09,097
My god, ew, the stench of him...

311
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:10,220
It's inside!

312
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:11,820
It's inside!

313
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,357
I'm trying, but I can't get in there.

314
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:19,377
I've gotten close enough
to feel the stand itself.

315
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:22,048
Wait, that repulsive
odor is coming from me.

316
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:24,120
Oh, your shoes.

317
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:26,517
Are they that dirty because of what I did?

318
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:27,537
My, I'm embarrassed.

319
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:28,500
How could I?

320
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:32,360
Here, please have a seat on this chair.

321
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,840
I'll let your shoes clean for you.

322
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:37,757
While you're waiting,

323
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:41,397
would you like to read the manga
I swiped from the guards' room?

324
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,009
Be careful, there's a bee.

325
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:45,037
Let me tell you about my master.

326
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:46,980
First off, his name is D and G.

327
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:50,077
The last I saw him, he was
in the discipline ward.

328
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:54,513
His left arm was a bleeding mess, and
he was bawling like a helpless baby.

329
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,920
I am Long Range Control Stand!

330
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:04,633
It's plenty to take the fruit
and run back to its master!

331
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:05,970
I noticed.

332
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,137
I'll be out here in a minute.

333
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:10,857
Jolene, we have to get
out of here right now.

334
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:12,217
Let's go to the marshland.

335
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:15,535
There might be a boat or at
least a water scooter there

336
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:22,097
Here's how to differentiate
wild strawberries.

337
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:26,280
The yellow one is only a mock
strawberry So you really can't eat it.

338
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:29,220
Do you ever shut the
fuck up? Wait a second.

339
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:31,657
We can't leave that stand where it is.

340
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:35,337
He swallowed the green plant, baby And
we have to get it out of him like now.

341
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:36,250
Right, I know

342
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:40,097
FF, tell that weirdo we
have to take him with us.

343
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:41,757
You have to go find the main body.

344
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,657
And when you do, blow him off the map.

345
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:44,740
It's my pleasure.

346
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,557
So I should go along with you?

347
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:48,400
Is that right, Master? Goody.

348
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:56,680
This is the exclusive
Marshland boat, Master.

349
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:58,217
You're going to love it.

350
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:01,497
It has a special propeller
powered by the wind to sail it.

351
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,933
You might be surprised how fast it goes.

352
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,010
Damn.

353
00:21:05,093 --> 00:21:05,923
What about the engine?

354
00:21:06,006 --> 00:21:06,939
How do I start it?

355
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:09,178
Is it locked on this boat somewhere?

356
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,037
It's the throttle lever, Master.

357
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:12,414
Here, let me show you.

358
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:16,952
If you want to get it in gear, you must
shift it in neutral first, like so.

359
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,037
The stick is the rudder.

360
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:24,537
Push it forward, the empanage,
or tail assembly turns right.

361
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:26,397
Pull it back, it turns to the left.

362
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,800
Simple as that. Ready?

363
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:29,537
Yes, untie the anchor rope, weirdo.

364
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:31,032
Yes, right away, Master.

365
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:41,320
Jolene, don't you dare take
your eyes off that stand.

366
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:52,253
As long as you've got him under your
watch, he'll be an excellent servant.

367
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:53,360
Perfect, even.

368
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:56,700
He's creepy, but he'll be useful.

369
00:21:57,480 --> 00:22:00,600
However, if you give him any leeway...

370
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,140
This son of a bitch!

371
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,560
This is way worse than I imagined!

372
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:13,790
Jolene...

373
00:22:13,873 --> 00:22:14,703
Anastasia...

374
00:22:14,786 --> 00:22:17,060
Don't take your eyes off
this monster for a second!

375
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:30,160
Although you think I cope

376
00:22:31,780 --> 00:22:35,160
My head is filled with hope

377
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:40,240
Of some place

378
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:43,400
Other than he

379
00:22:47,060 --> 00:22:50,177
Although you think I smile

380
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:55,337
inside and all the while,

381
00:22:55,420 --> 00:22:59,537
I'm wondering

382
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:03,400
about my destiny.

383
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:07,877
I'm thinking

384
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:13,557
about all the

385
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:18,417
things I'd like

386
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:24,440
to do in my life.

387
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:29,340
I'm a dreamer.

388
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:34,420
A distant dreamer.

389
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:39,400
Dreaming far away.

390
00:23:41,740 --> 00:23:44,540
From today!

391
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,270
Thank you.

392
00:24:31,660 --> 00:24:33,020
Thank you.
